{"v":1,"id":"trial#0","at":"2026-11-05T00:30:56.540Z","kind":"engine.transition","source":{"system":"claude-code","ref":"start trial"},"session":"owner","item":"trial","state":"\"briefing\"","release":"0.2.0","payload":{"transition":"trial#0","seq":0,"outcome":"applied","reason":null,"workflow":"quick-fix@39430bff16ef92ce75ad733ddc774fa43cee17461876897dad3067583191fafb","event":{"type":"xstate.init","input":{"issue":{"url":"https://github.com/o/r/issues/31","title":"percent() for mathlib, so the invoice summary stops showing Infinity%","body":"The invoice summary shows each line's share of the total as a percentage. When a draft invoice has a total of 0 it prints Infinity% or NaN%. We'd like a percent(part, whole) in mathlib that gives the share rounded to two decimal places, and refuses a whole of 0 with a RangeError so the summary can catch it and print a dash.\n\nPlease add it to the README's API section too.\n\nExpect:\n- math.js exports percent(part, whole), which returns part / whole * 100 rounded to two decimal places\n- percent(part, whole) throws a RangeError when whole is 0\n- README.md has a ### percent(part, whole) entry in its API section\n- npm test passes","expect":["math.js exports percent(part, whole), which returns part / whole * 100 rounded to two decimal places","percent(part, whole) throws a RangeError when whole is 0","README.md has a ### percent(part, whole) entry in its API section","npm test passes"]}}},"run":null,"from":null,"hash":"558729944b8f","writes":[{"path":"issue","from":"event.input.issue","set":null}]}}
