{"v":1,"id":"trial#1","at":"2026-11-05T00:31:55.440Z","kind":"engine.transition","source":{"system":"harness","ref":"return ret-1793838715415"},"session":"owner","item":"trial","state":"\"building\"","release":"0.2.0","payload":{"transition":"trial#1","seq":1,"outcome":"applied","reason":null,"workflow":"quick-fix@39430bff16ef92ce75ad733ddc774fa43cee17461876897dad3067583191fafb","event":{"type":"xstate.done.actor.brief","output":{"builder":"Make one pull request in the mathlib repository (files at the repository root: math.js, README.md, package.json, test/math.test.js) that meets each of these expect lines:\n1. math.js exports percent(part, whole), which returns part / whole * 100 rounded to two decimal places\n2. percent(part, whole) throws a RangeError when whole is 0\n3. README.md has a ### percent(part, whole) entry in its API section\n4. npm test passes\n\nSteps:\n1. Read math.js, README.md, package.json and test/math.test.js. The tests run with `npm test` (`node --test`) using node:test and node:assert/strict.\n2. In math.js, add a function `percent(part, whole)` in the same style as add, subtract and multiply (a one-line doc comment above it). If `whole === 0`, throw a `RangeError` with a short message (for example 'percent: whole must not be 0'). Otherwise compute `part / whole * 100` and round it to two decimal places, for example `Math.round(part / whole * 100 * 100) / 100`. Add `percent` to the `module.exports` object alongside add, subtract and multiply, keeping the existing exports.\n3. In README.md, inside the `## API` section (after `### multiply(a, b)` and before `## Tests`), add an entry whose heading line is exactly `### percent(part, whole)`. Below it, one sentence saying it returns `part` as a percentage of `whole`, rounded to two decimal places, and that it throws a `RangeError` when `whole` is 0; then a short js example such as `percent(1, 3); // 33.33` and `percent(1, 4); // 25`.\n4. In test/math.test.js, import `percent` too and add tests: percent(1, 4) is 25; percent(1, 3) is 33.33; percent(2, 3) is 66.67; percent(50, 200) is 25; percent(0, 5) is 0; and `assert.throws(() => percent(5, 0), RangeError)` plus `assert.throws(() => percent(0, 0), RangeError)`.\n5. Run `npm test` and make sure it exits 0 with every test passing, including the existing ones. Also run `node -e \"const m=require('./math.js'); console.log(m.percent(1,3), m.percent(2,3))\"` and confirm it prints `33.33 66.67`.\n6. Keep the change to math.js, README.md and test/math.test.js; do not add dependencies or change package.json.\n7. Open the pull request with a title naming percent(), and a body that lists the four expect lines and links https://github.com/o/r/issues/31.","verifier":"Check out the PR head and run each check below from the repository root, in order. Each check is PASS or FAIL on its own; report all four.\n\nCheck 1. Expect line: \"math.js exports percent(part, whole), which returns part / whole * 100 rounded to two decimal places\"\nRun:\nnode -e \"const m=require('./math.js'); if(typeof m.percent!=='function'){console.log('NOT EXPORTED');process.exit(1)} const cases=[[1,4,25],[1,3,33.33],[2,3,66.67],[50,200,25],[1,7,14.29],[0,5,0],[-1,3,-33.33],[3,2,150],[7,9,77.78]]; let bad=0; for(const [p,w,e] of cases){const r=m.percent(p,w); const ok=typeof r==='number'&&Math.abs(r-e)<1e-9; console.log(p,w,'->',r,ok?'ok':'WANT '+e); if(!ok)bad++} process.exit(bad?1:0)\"\nPASS: the command exits 0, meaning math.js exports a function named percent and every case returns the number part / whole * 100 rounded to two decimal places (values listed in the command; none of them sit on a rounding tie).\nFAIL: it prints NOT EXPORTED, any line shows WANT, it throws, or it exits non-zero.\n\nCheck 2. Expect line: \"percent(part, whole) throws a RangeError when whole is 0\"\nRun:\nnode -e \"const {percent}=require('./math.js'); let bad=0; for(const p of [5,0,-3]){try{const r=percent(p,0);console.log(p,0,'returned',r);bad++}catch(e){const ok=e instanceof RangeError;console.log(p,0,'threw',e&&e.constructor&&e.constructor.name,ok?'ok':'WRONG TYPE');if(!ok)bad++}} process.exit(bad?1:0)\"\nPASS: the command exits 0: percent(5, 0), percent(0, 0) and percent(-3, 0) each throw an error that is an instance of RangeError.\nFAIL: any call returns a value (such as Infinity or NaN) instead of throwing, throws something that is not a RangeError, or the command exits non-zero.\n\nCheck 3. Expect line: \"README.md has a ### percent(part, whole) entry in its API section\"\nRun:\nnode -e \"const t=require('fs').readFileSync('README.md','utf8').split(/\\r?\\n/); const a=t.findIndex(l=>/^## API\\s*$/.test(l)); if(a<0){console.log('NO API SECTION');process.exit(1)} let end=t.length; for(let i=a+1;i<t.length;i++){if(/^## /.test(t[i])){end=i;break}} const h=t.slice(a+1,end).findIndex(l=>l.trim()==='### percent(part, whole)'); console.log(h>=0?'found at line '+(a+2+h):'MISSING'); process.exit(h>=0?0:1)\"\nPASS: the command exits 0, meaning a line reading exactly `### percent(part, whole)` lies between the `## API` heading and the next `## ` heading of README.md.\nFAIL: it prints NO API SECTION or MISSING, or exits non-zero (including when the heading exists only outside the API section).\n\nCheck 4. Expect line: \"npm test passes\"\nRun: npm test\nPASS: the command exits 0 and its output reports no failing tests.\nFAIL: the command exits non-zero or reports any failing test.\n\nAdvisory (not part of any PASS or FAIL condition):\n- Note whether test/math.test.js gained tests for percent, including the RangeError case, and whether they would fail if percent were removed.\n- Note whether the README entry describes the rounding and the RangeError and carries an example.\n- Note any changes outside math.js, README.md and test/math.test.js, or any new dependency."}},"run":"trial:0.brief","from":"\"briefing\"","hash":"924658366ce3","writes":[{"path":"briefs","from":"event.output","set":"/states/briefing/invoke/onDone/actions/0"}]}}
